====================================================================================================
HOW TO READ THIS
====================================================================================================
  JOINT PASS => the blocker was never a shape at all: the clipper turns on too LATE along the
  DRIVE sweep, and K/clipSat/clipA0 are ONE degenerate family that must be fit TOGETHER.
  Session 15's two 'degenerate corner' rejections should then be re-read as the optimiser
  correctly reporting an onset error while K was frozen at an adopted, unmeasured value —
  i.e. the physicality test was applied to clipSat alone, half of a degenerate pair.
  Session 17 would re-fit with K in the parameter set and judge physicality on the PAIR
  (implied input volts AND clipSat volts), never on clipSat with K pinned.
  FAIL => onset position is not it either; with taper, rails and onset all refuted, the
  remaining candidate on the drive axis is a drive-dependent MEMORY effect (clipper input
  coupling: GRUNT cap bank + R16), which no memoryless VTC can produce — §3u.6's fallback.
